  "summary_text": "**Context Note: Chartkite Launch Strategy – Finalized Decisions, Open Threads, and Framework (As of May 2025)**\n\nChartkite is feature-complete and preparing for launch. The following is a comprehensive, retrieval-friendly summary of all decisions, trade-offs, constraints, and frameworks established in this conversation.\n\n---\n\n### ✅ **Decisions Made & Alternatives Rejected**\n\n- **Pricing Model**: Chosen: **Usage-based with prepaid credits** (e.g., users buy 100 credits, spend per chart/query).  \n  - *Rejected*:  \n    - Flat monthly fee per workspace (too rigid, doesn’t scale with user behavior)  \n    - Per-seat tiers (creates friction for solo users, misaligns with cost structure)  \n  - *Why*: Matches infrastructure cost scaling, supports experimentation, feels fair and value-driven.\n\n- **Onboarding Flow (Nimbus)**: Chosen: **No blank dashboard. Real, interactive chart on landing. One-click \"Try a Chart\" button. No pop-ups, no tours, no forms.**  \n  - *Rejected*:  \n    - Guidely-style in-app tours (91% dismissal rate in testing)  \n    - Pre-connection gate (requires data source before login)  \n    - Step-by-step walkthroughs (feels like a tutorial)  \n  - *Why*: Prioritizes immediate value, human-first experience, and low friction.\n\n- **Launch Sequence**: Chosen: **Invite-only beta with 30 design partners**.  \n  - *Rejected*:  \n    - Public splash (too noisy, high risk of bad first impression)  \n    - Webinars (91% user drop-off in testing)  \n    - Countdown timers (considered scammy, against brand values)  \n  - *Why*: Builds authentic social proof, ensures real-world usage, protects brand trust.\n\n- **Marketing & Outreach**: Chosen: **No trade publication pitching**, **no cold email campaigns** (0.4% reply rate, 2 spam complaints in past quarter).  \n  - *Why*: Low signal, high noise. Effort better spent on beta validation and organic growth.\n\n- **Metrics Dashboard (Founder View)**: Chosen: **5 core metrics**  \n  1. Active users (24h)  \n  2. First-chart conversion rate (Nimbus)  \n  3. Average time to first chart  \n  4. Report shipments (charts created, 7-day)  \n  5. Credit usage per user (to monitor for abuse or underuse)  \n  - *Why*: Tracks activation, retention, and value delivery — not vanity.\n\n---\n\n### 🔑 **Key Terms & Definitions**\n\n- **Nimbus**: The self-serve signup and onboarding funnel — from landing page to first login. *Not* the cloud migration (that’s \"Infra-Relay\").  \n- **TM-88214**: Trademark filing reference (submitted April 9). Expected issuance: 12–18 months.  \n- **Cloud Budget Cap**: $6,410/month. Must not be exceeded.  \n- **Design Partners**: 30 invited users who must ship one real report before public access.  \n- **Usage-based pricing**: Users prepay for credits; spend per chart/query. No per-seat or flat fee.\n\n---\n\n### ⚠️ **Open Threads & Next Steps**\n\n- Finalize Nimbus copy: Replace all tutorial language, remove \"connect data\" as barrier. Use action-first, visual language.  \n- Define \"report shipment\" metric: Must be tied to a user’s first chart that they *share or export*.  \n- Draft invite email for design partners: Must emphasize \"ship a real report\" as the goal.  \n- Build dashboard for founder: 5 metrics, real-time, updated daily.\n\n---\n\n### ❌ **Options Tried and Ruled Out**\n\n- **Guidely in-app tours**: 91% dismissal rate in testing → removed.  \n- **Cold email campaigns (via Prospexo)**: 0.4% reply rate, 2 spam complaints → permanently closed.  \n- **Trade publication outreach**: High rejection rate, low credibility for small tools → not pursued.  \n- **Countdown timers, webinars, pop-up tours**: All rejected as \"sc",
